Hi Isaac,

The variances for the latent variables (e.g., l_one) intermediate between latent_g and the items would need to be modeled. I got an error message that the standard errors could not be computed when those latent variables were unstandardized, but no problems when they were standardized. Please see the MWE below.

Best wishes,
Wen Wei
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
library("lavaan")
pop.model <- '
latent_g=~0.7*l_one+0.7*l_two+0.7*l_three
l_one=~1*one
l_two=~1*two
l_three=~1*three

one~~0.8*one
two~~0.8*two
three~~0.8*three
'
D <- simulateData(pop.model, std.lv <http://std.lv>=FALSE, empirical=TRUE)
model <- '

latent_g=~l_one+l_two+l_three
l_one=~1*one
l_two=~1*two
l_three=~1*three

one~~e1*one
two~~e2*two
three~~e3*three

'

fit <- lavaan::sem(model,data=D, std.lv <http://std.lv>=FALSE)
parameterEstimates(fit)

fit <- lavaan::sem(model,data=D, std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE)
parameterEstimates(fit)

